   "title": "Your Villages Weekend + What's New: Rocky, Smash Burgers & Soft Serve",
   "date": "July 16, 2026 · By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider",
   "body": "<p>Well, friends, we made it to another Thursday. The golf cart is charged, the wine is chilled, and I've done my homework so you don't have to. Here's the scoop on the weekend ahead &mdash; plus a few new things around town worth knowing about.</p>\n\n<p>Quick reminder: summer hours are still in effect on the squares. Through September 30, the nightly music runs <strong>6 to 10 p.m.</strong> instead of 5 to 9, per <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/entertainment-summer-hours/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Villages Entertainment</a>. Happy hour at the bar huts hasn't moved &mdash; still 5 to 6. Get there early, grab your drink, claim your spot.</p>\n\n<h3>Friday, July 17</h3>\n<p>The big one: <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Rocky and The Rollers</strong> take over Brownwood Paddock Square</a>. Twenty-seven years playing The Villages, and they still pack the place every time. Trust me on this one. If you're heading there, eat early &mdash; the Brownwood restaurants fill up fast on Rocky nights.</p>\n<p>Elsewhere Friday: Radlin' Rootz at Spanish Springs, The Edge Of Rock (our own homegrown rockers) at Lake Sumter Landing, 5.0.1. playing blues and soul at Sawgrass Grove, and Osaka Fall at Eastport. All 6 to 10 p.m.</p>\n\n<h3>Saturday, July 18</h3>\n<p>Saturday is a doubleheader at Sawgrass Grove. <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Handpicked Trio plays bluegrass from noon to 3</a> &mdash; fiddle, banjo, the works. Perfect excuse for a long lunch at The Market. Then Cable Cars takes the evening shift at 6.</p>\n<p>On the squares: September Dogs at Spanish Springs (female-fronted, great layered vocals), The Fire Rhythms Band at Lake Sumter Landing with those Caribbean and Brazilian beats, and The Voodoo Gypsies doing '60s-'70s-'80s rock at Brownwood.</p>\n\n<h3>Sunday, July 19</h3>\n<p>There's live music on every square Sunday night too, 6 to 10 as always. The <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">official calendar</a> has the full slate &mdash; check it before you roll out.</p>\n<p>One more thing while you're out: the bar huts are pouring a <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/bar-huts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><strong>Freedom Punch</strong> special all July</a> &mdash; red, white, and blue, $8 single, $10.50 double, while supplies last. I had a sip of my neighbor's. Sweet, cold, and dangerous in the best way.</p>\n\n<h3>What's new around town</h3>\n<p><strong>The hottest nightspot in town serves soft serve.</strong> The new Twistee Treat at Pinellas Plaza &mdash; the first one inside The Villages &mdash; <a href=\"https://www.thevillages.com/whats-new/shopping-dining/twistee-treat-open-the-villages/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">opened July 1 on Burnsed Boulevard</a>, and Villages-News reports the <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/15/hottest-new-nightspot-in-the-villages-isnt-serving-booze/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">lines of carts and cars at night</a> are something to behold. It's the cone-shaped building you can't miss. Cones, twirls, slushies, shakes, sundaes. No booze, no cover charge, no complaints. You're welcome.</p>\n<p><strong>Three new food counters coming to Sawgrass Grove.</strong> FMK &mdash; the folks behind Luma &mdash; is <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/06/fmk-bringing-new-food-selections-to-market-at-sawgrass-grove/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">adding three new spots to The Market at Sawgrass Grove</a>: Sizzle 'N Smash (smash burgers and milkshakes), Southern Tender (chicken tenders and fries), and Papa Joe's Pizza and More (by the slice or whole pie). Between these and Saturday's bluegrass lunch, Sawgrass Grove is making a real case for itself.</p>\n<p><strong>A new ER is nearly here.</strong> AdventHealth has <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/13/opening-date-announced-for-new-adventhealth-er-on-county-road-466a/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">announced the opening date</a> for its new freestanding emergency room on County Road 466A near Colony Plaza &mdash; a $20 million, 12-room facility. Nobody wants to need it, but it's awfully good to have close by. The Villages-News piece has the date and details.</p>\n<p><strong>End of an era on Main Street.</strong> Citizens First Bank &mdash; The Villages' hometown bank since the beginning &mdash; has <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/11/end-of-an-era-as-the-villages-hometown-bank-officially-changes-ownership/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">officially changed ownership</a>. The branches are still there and life goes on, but for those of us who remember when it was the only bank in town, it's a moment. Raise a Freedom Punch to the old girl.</p>\n\n<p>That's the week, friends. Pencil in Rocky on Friday, bluegrass and a smash burger rumor on Saturday, and a Twistee Treat cone whenever the mood strikes &mdash; which, if you're me, is Tuesday. And Thursday. And possibly tonight.</p>\n<p>See you around the square,<br>&mdash; Susan</p>"
  },
