   "title": "Your Villages Weekend Recap: Clark Barrios, Storm Skies & More",
   "date": "July 13, 2026 · By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider",
   "body": "<p>Happy Monday, neighbors. Grab your coffee &mdash; here's the scoop on the weekend we just had.</p>\n\n<p>First, a housekeeping note if you haven't been out to the squares lately. Summer hours are still in effect &mdash; music runs <strong>6 to 10 p.m.</strong> through the end of September, per <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Villages Entertainment</a>. That extra hour past nine takes some getting used to. But it beats melting at 5 o'clock. Trust me on this one.</p>\n\n<h3>Friday night: DJ night at Brownwood</h3>\n<p>Friday, <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Brownwood Paddock Square went full club mode with DJ Lu-S</a> spinning until 10. Not everybody's cup of tea, I know. But the younger crowd &mdash; and by younger I mean the 60-somethings &mdash; seems to love a DJ night. The Greg Warren Trio held down the south end of town with their country and classic rock mix.</p>\n\n<h3>Saturday: a full slate on the squares</h3>\n<p>Saturday was the big one. The <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Clark Barrios Band</a> played Brownwood &mdash; six pieces, big vocals, the kind of rhythm section that gets golf carts parked early. Over at Spanish Springs, Zee-R brought his family-friendly classics from all eras. He's originally from Brazil, and his shows always draw a friendly crowd. And Lake Sumter Landing had a homegrown Villages rock band cranking out classic rock favorites right in my backyard.</p>\n<p>Mother Nature put on her own show Saturday night, too. If you saw those clouds flickering over Lake Sumter, you weren't imagining it &mdash; <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/12/nighttime-storm-clouds-light-up-over-lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Villages-News caught the nighttime storm clouds lighting up over Lake Sumter Landing</a>. July in Florida, folks. Keep the rain jacket in the cart.</p>\n\n<h3>While you're at the square: Freedom Punch</h3>\n<p>Here's one for my fellow snackers and sippers. The bar huts on the squares are pouring a <strong>Freedom Punch</strong> all July &mdash; red, white, and blue, served over ice, $8 for a single and $10.50 for a double, <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/bar-huts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">while supplies last</a>. The Tequila Sunrise is still on the menu at the same price if punch isn't your thing. You're welcome.</p>\n\n<h3>The end of an era</h3>\n<p>Some real hometown news from the weekend: <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/11/end-of-an-era-as-the-villages-hometown-bank-officially-changes-ownership/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Villages-News reported Saturday</a> that our hometown bank has officially changed ownership. An end of an era for a lot of us who've banked there since we unpacked our first moving box. I'll keep an ear out on what changes &mdash; if anything &mdash; for us regulars.</p>\n\n<h3>One from Susan's little black book</h3>\n<p>Filed under &ldquo;who knew?&rdquo; &mdash; there's a <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/12/residents-can-take-part-in-free-program-to-learn-about-safe-internet-browsing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">free program to learn safe internet browsing</a> open to residents. With all the scam calls and phishing emails going around, this one's worth an hour of your time. I sent my own neighbor. Details are in the Villages-News writeup.</p>\n<p>And a little something for the bird lovers: a Villages-News photographer caught a <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/11/swallow-tailed-kite-feeds-on-midair-catch-over-sawgrass-grove/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">swallow-tailed kite feeding on a midair catch over Sawgrass Grove</a> this weekend. Gorgeous shot. Worth a click.</p>\n\n<h3>Looking ahead this week</h3>\n<p>Tonight it's <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">X Girlfriend at Brownwood, Big Chief at Spanish Springs, Earth Beat at Lake Sumter Landing, and live band karaoke at Eastport</a> &mdash; yes, you singing with a real band behind you. And Sawgrass Grove has Boozy Bingo tonight and free Trivia Tuesday at noon tomorrow.</p>\n\n<p>That's the weekend, friends. Short, sweet, and true.</p>\n<p>See you around the square,<br>&mdash; Susan</p>"
  },
