   "title": "Your Villages Weekend + What's New: Soul at the Savannah",
   "date": "July 9, 2026 · By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider",
   "body": "<p>Here's the scoop, friends. July is doing its July thing &mdash; steamy afternoons, quick storms, and that golden hour when the squares come alive. The good news? Nightly entertainment runs 6 to 10 p.m. all summer now, <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/nightly-entertainment/\">pushed back an hour to dodge the heat</a>. Smart move. That's one more hour for dinner before the dancing starts.</p>\n\n<h3>What to do this weekend</h3>\n<p><strong>Friday night: pick your square.</strong> At Spanish Springs, <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/spanish-springs/\">Bandemic</a> takes the stage from 6 to 10 with forty-plus years of rock, from classic '80s to country-rock. Down at Brownwood, <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood-paddock-square/\">The Brothers Jukebox</a> brings country gold and classic rock harmonies, same hours. I lean Brownwood on Fridays. Grab an early table on the square, then wander over when the band kicks in.</p>\n<p><strong>Saturday morning: the farmers market.</strong> The <a href=\"https://www.thevillages.com/whats-new/health-wellness/visit-brownwood-farmers-market/\">Brownwood Farmers Market</a> runs Saturday from 9 to 1 &mdash; summer hours, so go early before the produce wilts and so do you. Fresh vegetables, local honey, baked goods. I never leave empty-handed. Trust me on this one.</p>\n<p><strong>Saturday night: the big one.</strong> <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/ticketed-performances/a-decade-of-soul/\">A Decade of Soul</a> plays the Savannah Center on Saturday. This is the Motown and '70s soul tribute that ran more than 1,600 shows in Times Square before finding its way to us. Aretha, Marvin, James Brown &mdash; the whole songbook. It's ticketed, so check times and grab seats through The Villages Entertainment before it sells through.</p>\n<p>Rather stay outside Saturday? <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/spanish-springs/\">The Edge Of Rock</a> &mdash; a homegrown Villages rock band &mdash; plays Spanish Springs, and the <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood-paddock-square/\">Zee-R Band</a> covers classic hits at Brownwood, both 6 to 10.</p>\n<p><strong>Sunday: ease into it.</strong> <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/spanish-springs/\">Think Big Band</a> plays Spanish Springs from 6 to 10 &mdash; classic rock, Motown, blues, country, they play it all. Over at Brownwood, the <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/brownwood-paddock-square/\">Alex Hayes Band</a> brings high-energy country rock. A Sunday supper near either square, then an hour or two of music? That's my kind of weekend landing.</p>\n<p>One more thing while you're out there: the bar huts are pouring a <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/bar-huts/\">Freedom Punch</a> special through July &mdash; red, white, and blue in a cup, $8 single. You're welcome.</p>\n\n<h3>What's new</h3>\n<p><strong>More food coming to The Market at Sawgrass Grove.</strong> This is the one I'm excited about. FMK &mdash; the folks behind Luma Mediterranean Kitchen &mdash; announced <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/07/06/fmk-bringing-new-food-selections-to-market-at-sawgrass-grove/\">three new food spots for the Market</a>: Sizzle 'N Smash for smash burgers and milkshakes, Southern Tender for chicken tenders and fries, and Papa Joe's Pizza and More with pizza by the slice. Luma won me over on the first visit, so I have high hopes. The grandkids will be thrilled about the milkshakes. So will I, frankly.</p>\n<p><strong>Zunzibar is open in Middleton.</strong> A new restaurant called <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/06/20/new-restaurant-opening-monday-in-middleton/\">Zunzibar opened in Middleton late last month</a>. I haven't made it down yet, but it's on my list. If you've been, tell me what to order.</p>\n<p><strong>The new Walmart on 466 is open.</strong> The <a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/2026/06/24/early-birds-out-in-force-for-opening-of-new-walmart/\">new Walmart in Lady Lake opened June 24</a> at the Hammock Oaks development on County Road 466, and the early birds were out in force. Handy if you're on the north side. The parking lot is still finding its rhythm, so maybe skip the Saturday noon rush.</p>\n\n<p>That's the weekend, neighbors. Music every night, soul on Saturday, and burgers on the horizon. Pencil it in.</p>\n<p>See you around the square,<br>&mdash; Susan</p>"
