   "title": "Your Villages Weekend Recap: Rocky, Jazz & a Warm One",
   "date": "June 29, 2026 · By Susan Whitfield, Villages insider",
   "body": "<p>Well, hello again. Pull up a chair. I hope you got out this weekend, because the squares were humming. It was a warm one &mdash; central Florida in late June, you know the drill &mdash; but the music didn't mind one bit. Here's the scoop on what I caught.</p>\n\n<h3>The squares were singing</h3>\n<p>Friday night I made my way down to <strong>Lake Sumter Landing</strong>, and who do I find but <strong>Rocky and The Rollers</strong> &mdash; 27 years of doing this in The Villages and still packing the dance floor. They closed out the weekend Sunday night too. If you like your oldies high-energy with a little doo-wop sparkle, those are your guys. Saturday the Landing switched it up with <strong>Osaka Fall</strong>, who run everything from old-school jams to glam rock and soulful slow ones. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/lake-sumter-landing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Lake Sumter Landing schedule</a>)</p>\n<p>Over at <strong>Sawgrass Grove</strong>, Friday belonged to <strong>3P</strong>, that acoustic trio that bounces between reggae, country and pop without missing a step. Saturday brought in <strong>Radlin' Rootz</strong>, an eclectic band of top-tier players out of Ocala. Those same Rootz folks turned up Sunday at <strong>Spanish Springs</strong> &mdash; so if you missed them one night, the square gods gave you a second chance. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/sawgrass-grove/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Sawgrass Grove</a>, <a href=\"https://www.thevillagesentertainment.com/spanish-springs/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Spanish Springs</a>)</p>\n<p>And <strong>Brownwood</strong> kept the Saturday crowd on their feet with a Motown-and-Top-40 set built for dancing. The squares run music every single night, 6 to 10, and it's free &mdash; still the best deal in town. (<a href=\"https://www.villages-news.com/category/town-square-entertainment/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Live Square Entertainment</a>)</p>\n\n<h3>A little something indoors, too</h3>\n<p>Not everyone wants to sweat through a square dance in June, and I don't blame you. Saturday night, <strong>Savannah Center</strong> hosted <strong>3DN &mdash; The Ultimate 3 Dog Nite Tribute Show</strong>. If &ldquo;Joy to the World&rdquo; is still on your car radio, that was the ticket. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesdailysun.com/calendar/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Daily Sun calendar</a>)</p>\n<p>Here's my who-knew note for the weekend. Sunday evening, <strong>More Jazz</strong> brought the <strong>Rick Steuart Quartet</strong> to <strong>Colony Cottage Recreation Center</strong>. A quiet, classy night of jazz tucked into a rec center &mdash; that's the kind of thing folks live here for years and never try. Trust me on this one: the smaller rec-center shows are some of the best-kept secrets we've got. (<a href=\"https://www.eventbrite.com/d/fl--the-villages/events/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">events listing</a>)</p>\n\n<h3>Eating around the music</h3>\n<p>I won't pretend I tracked down a brand-new restaurant opening this weekend &mdash; I didn't, and I won't make one up for you. But the squares make their own dinner plan. Grab a bite at the Landing or Sawgrass before the band starts, find a spot with a little shade, and let the night come to you. That's the move when it's this warm out.</p>\n<p>Speaking of warm &mdash; let's be honest about it. We sat in the low-to-mid 90s all weekend with the usual afternoon thunderstorms rolling through. (<a href=\"https://www.accuweather.com/en/us/the-villages/32159/weather-forecast/2257923\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AccuWeather</a>) Keep water in the cart, find the late-day breeze, and don't fight the heat &mdash; outlast it. The music doesn't get going till the sun's on its way down anyway.</p>\n\n<h3>Looking ahead</h3>\n<p>If you're already itching for the week, <strong>1776 the Musical</strong> takes the stage at Savannah Center tonight, Monday, at 7. (<a href=\"https://www.thevillagesdailysun.com/calendar/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Daily Sun calendar</a>) A little patriotic warm-up before the Fourth.</p>\n<p>That's what I could confirm from a warm, music-filled weekend. Quieter on the big-event front, but the squares carried it like they always do. Now go enjoy yourself.</p>\n<p>See you around the square,<br>&mdash; Susan</p>"
  },
